      "summaries": {
        "en": "Vaultwarden is a lightweight, self-hosted password manager server compatible with Bitwarden clients. It solves the need for a private, resource-efficient alternative to the official Bitwarden server. Written in Rust, it uses minimal memory and CPU, making it ideal for low-power devices like Raspberry Pi. You can deploy it via Docker in minutes, sync passwords across devices, and maintain full control over your data. Perfect for individuals or small teams seeking a secure, open-source password management solution without cloud dependencies.",
        "zh": "Vaultwarden 是一个轻量级、自托管的密码管理器服务器，兼容 Bitwarden 客户端。它解决了官方服务器资源占用高的问题，让你在低功耗设备（如树莓派）上也能运行。核心优势在于用 Rust 编写，内存和 CPU 消耗极低，且完全开源。通过 Docker 几分钟即可部署，支持多设备同步密码、自动填充等功能。适合个人或小团队，既享受 Bitwarden 生态的便利，又保持数据完全自主可控。你可以用它搭建家庭或团队的密码管理中枢，无需依赖任何云服务。",
        "es": "Vaultwarden is a lightweight, self-hosted password manager server compatible with Bitwarden clients. It solves the need for a private, resource-efficient alternative to the official Bitwarden server. Written in Rust, it uses minimal memory and CPU, making it ideal for low-power devices like Raspberry Pi. You can deploy it via Docker in minutes, sync passwords across devices, and maintain full control over your data. Perfect for individuals or small teams seeking a secure, open-source password management solution without cloud dependencies.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "vaultwarden stands out for bitwarden, bitwarden-rs, and docker in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Vaultwarden is a lightweight, self-hosted password manager server compatible with Bitwarden clients. It solves the need for a private, resource-efficient alternative to the official Bitwarden server. Written in Rust, it uses minimal memory and CPU, making it ideal for low-power devices like Raspberry Pi. You can deploy it via Docker in minutes, sync passwords across devices, and maintain full control over your data. Perfect for individuals or small teams seeking a secure, open-source password management solution without cloud dependencies.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/dani-garcia/vaultwarden for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
