      "summaries": {
        "en": "typescript-go is a staging repository for Microsoft's experimental native port of the TypeScript compiler from TypeScript/JavaScript to Go. This project aims to significantly improve compiler performance and reduce memory usage by leveraging Go's concurrency and efficient runtime. The key technical insight is that rewriting performance-critical infrastructure in a systems language like Go can yield substantial speedups while maintaining full compatibility. Developers can follow the development, contribute, or test early builds to experience faster type-checking and compilation in their workflows.",
        "zh": "typescript-go 是微软将 TypeScript 编译器从 TypeScript/JavaScript 原生移植到 Go 语言的实验性项目。其核心目标是利用 Go 的并发模型和高效运行时，大幅提升编译性能并降低内存占用。技术亮点在于：将性能关键的基础设施用系统级语言重写，可在保持完全兼容的前提下获得显著加速。开发者可以关注开发进展、参与贡献或测试早期构建版本，体验更快的类型检查和编译速度。这一项目展示了如何通过语言迁移优化现有工具链，为大型代码库的构建效率带来质的提升。",
        "es": "typescript-go is a staging repository for Microsoft's experimental native port of the TypeScript compiler from TypeScript/JavaScript to Go. This project aims to significantly improve compiler performance and reduce memory usage by leveraging Go's concurrency and efficient runtime. The key technical insight is that rewriting performance-critical infrastructure in a systems language like Go can yield substantial speedups while maintaining full compatibility. Developers can follow the development, contribute, or test early builds to experience faster type-checking and compilation in their workflows.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "typescript-go gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "typescript-go is a staging repository for Microsoft's experimental native port of the TypeScript compiler from TypeScript/JavaScript to Go. This project aims to significantly improve compiler performance and reduce memory usage by leveraging Go's concurrency and efficient runtime. The key technical insight is that rewriting performance-critical infrastructure in a systems language like Go can yield substantial speedups while maintaining full compatibility. Developers can follow the development, contribute, or test early builds to experience faster type-checking and compilation in their workflows.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/microsoft/typescript-go for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
