      "summaries": {
        "en": "OSV-Scanner is a vulnerability scanner that uses the open-source OSV.dev database to find known vulnerabilities in project dependencies. Its key strength is direct integration with the OSV database, providing accurate and up-to-date results without relying on local vulnerability feeds. Written in Go, it supports multiple ecosystems like npm, PyPI, and Go modules. You can run it as a CLI tool or integrate it into CI/CD pipelines to automatically check for vulnerabilities in your lockfiles or SBOMs, making security auditing simple and fast.",
        "zh": "OSV-Scanner 是一款基于 OSV.dev 数据库的开源漏洞扫描器，专门用于检测项目依赖中的已知安全漏洞。其核心优势在于直接对接 OSV 数据库，无需维护本地漏洞源即可获取最新、准确的扫描结果。工具采用 Go 语言编写，支持 npm、PyPI、Go 模块等多种生态系统的依赖格式。实际使用中，你可以通过命令行快速扫描项目的 lockfile 或 SBOM 文件，或将其集成到 CI/CD 流水线中实现自动化安全审计。这种设计让开发者能以极低门槛持续监控依赖风险，尤其适合需要快速集成漏洞检查的团队。",
        "es": "OSV-Scanner is a vulnerability scanner that uses the open-source OSV.dev database to find known vulnerabilities in project dependencies. Its key strength is direct integration with the OSV database, providing accurate and up-to-date results without relying on local vulnerability feeds. Written in Go, it supports multiple ecosystems like npm, PyPI, and Go modules. You can run it as a CLI tool or integrate it into CI/CD pipelines to automatically check for vulnerabilities in your lockfiles or SBOMs, making security auditing simple and fast.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "osv-scanner stands out for scanner, security-audit, and security-tools in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "OSV-Scanner is a vulnerability scanner that uses the open-source OSV.dev database to find known vulnerabilities in project dependencies. Its key strength is direct integration with the OSV database, providing accurate and up-to-date results without relying on local vulnerability feeds. Written in Go, it supports multiple ecosystems like npm, PyPI, and Go modules. You can run it as a CLI tool or integrate it into CI/CD pipelines to automatically check for vulnerabilities in your lockfiles or SBOMs, making security auditing simple and fast.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/google/osv-scanner for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
